Create a circuit that performs a multiplication operation on a 32-bit input. The module processes the input data by applying a series of bitwise shifts and subtractions to generate the output, effectively implementing a multiplication algorithm. Specifically, it computes the equivalent of multiplying the input by 64 (by shifting left) and adjusting the results using subtractive steps to achieve the desired multiplication outcome. The final result is a 32-bit output.
